A||N||21||1FST2M6||Doesn't look like a 4x4 anymore...||||1||
Z||000000||1FST2M6||11-07-2000||09:01 AM||||well after an hour of saying bad things to my car i got my stock springs out. the front were happy with where they lived and didn't want to vacate. I ploped in the new springs and turned the jack back down.. not realizing that since this car was lower than my SE the jack was gunna get stuck. so i got the jack out of the Saturn and re-jacked up the car to pull the floor jack out from under it.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif"> the back took about 20 minutes. it's 2.25" lower in all 4 corners on a progressive rate custom wound spring. rears are 910lb and the fronts are 730lb at their max compression. it gunna take a while to get used to .. cause you toss it into a corner and you KNOW your going straight in to the dirt but then the springs catch and POOF your turned and haulin' @$$ again... Bilstiens are sweet NO adjustments to mess with, just nice and sporty ride.. not teeth breaking and not Caddy ride. well what do ya think... <P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/1fsthydrant.jpg"> <P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/1fstlow.jpg"> <BR>||||reg||1
Z||000001||deceler8||11-07-2000||09:05 AM||||Gorgeous, man...just gorgeous.<P>Love the color...the black spoiler really sets it off and the wheels are perfect.||||reg||1
Z||000002||stsmithgt||11-07-2000||10:02 AM||||I like the idea of progressive springs over linear.  I think that's better than adjustable linear ones any day.  <P>I agree with D--8 about the wheels too.  They go well with the cool look of the fastback (my prefered favorite) <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>||||reg||14
Z||000003||Raydar||11-07-2000||10:25 AM||||Damn. Lins is STILL on that motorcycle! <BR>Watch it. She's gonna hafta have one!<P>The slam looks good. <BR>Looks like it was meant to be that way.<BR>Glad the ride is decent. <BR>I was picturing "conestoga wagon" in my mind.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/eek.gif"><BR>(Purely from an "old fart" point of view.)<P>Raydar||||reg||12
Z||000004||1FST2M6||11-07-2000||10:31 AM||||Yeah as long as she happy i can waste my money on the car.. so if she wants a bike i'll have to get two.. oh darn    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">   <P>We were REALLY surprised by how well it rides! yeah it's firm but not any worse then the Alfa! but if you throw it in a curve the springs REALLY do their job wel and then it's gets teeth breaking but that fine with me.. the tires don't scrub, and with more then 1 degre of negative camber it's really hard pressed to break loose! <BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/camber.jpg">   <BR> you can kinda see the camber in the rear... the tire should be nearly straigh up.. as you can see the top is tipped in the fender well a bit... (negative camber)<p>[This message has been edited by 1FST2M6 (edited 11-07-2000).]||||reg||1
