Z||000010||bHooper||11-08-2000||12:52 PM||||Travis, what does the 1* of neg camber do, as far as ridding around town?  Would there be any rubbing issues with stock rims and 215/60  front and 225/60 on the rear, with Eibach springs?  I have about decided to go with 1 tire size larger all the way around, with stock rims, although I may have to go with a 55 aspect ratio instead of the 60.<P>------------------<BR>hoop<BR>Red '86 GT||||reg||1
Z||000011||1FST2M6||11-08-2000||12:57 PM||||you will not have rubbing issues.. the SE has -1* of camber and has about 8000 miles on the tires now and jeff hasn't complained.. the only thing you'll have is better handeling in a tight corner and increased inner tire wear. but not so bad as you'd have to change them every 6 months... i'm very happy with it.. the Saturn has .75* the Alfa has 1* both in all 4 corners... ||||reg||1
Z||000012||bHooper||11-08-2000||01:51 PM||||i am doing everything necessary to make it easier for the alignment tech to set the camber... i am using Moog adj. upper ball joints, and cam bolts in the rear.<P>he should have no problem getting it set to -1*<P>------------------<BR>hoop<BR>Red '86 GT||||reg||1
Z||000013||1FST2M6||11-08-2000||01:53 PM||||None at all... the back will fall into place with the turn of a screw and the front the same...  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> ||||reg||1
